SUMMARY:Petaluma Art & Garden Festival
DESCRIPTION:One of Petaluma’s most cherished summer traditions! The 23rd Annual Art & Garden Festival is a vibrant\, family-friendly celebration of creativity\, community\, and local flavor. Each year\, over 15\,000 people fill the historic downtown to enjoy a lively day of art\, music\, food\, and fun. \nExplore more than 100 handpicked art exhibitors offering unique\, high-quality\, handmade goods – from garden and home décor to artisan jewelry and fine art. Live music will fill the air from two stages\, while local wineries\, breweries\, distilleries\, and restaurants serve up delicious tastes of Sonoma County and beyond. Gardening experts will be available to share tips on growing in our tricky adobe soil and making your garden truly organic. A Children’s Corner features jump houses\, face painting\, and free hands-on arts and crafts. \nThe festival takes place on Kentucky Street\, Fourth Street\, B Street\, and the A Street parking lot. Festival Headquarters will be located at the Petaluma Historical Library & Museum Garden Court\, 20 Fourth Street. \nAdmission is free\, with tasting packages available for those who wish to sample the amazing variety of wine\, craft beer\, cider\, cocktails\, and more. \nWe can’t wait to welcome you to downtown Petaluma this summer! \nPlease keep your furry friends at home ~ this event is very busy and typically warm. \nThis is not an ideal location for pets and could be overwhelming for your animal. \nEvent will be held rain or shine!
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/petaluma-art-garden-festival-2/
LOCATION:Historic Downtown Petaluma\, 20 4th Street\, Petaluma\, CA
CATEGORIES:Festival,Other
END:VEVENT
